## Largest unresolved evidence gap: the aunt (UNRES-01)

The draft's closing beat rests on an aunt who named him and is available to be asked — "Somewhere in South Carolina there's an aunt who knows exactly what 'Duke' means. He has had three decades to ask."

On the 2025-08-17 return stream, Duke attributed his month-long absence to both the San Antonio arrest **and grief over his aunt's death in July 2025**. The draft's working notes flag this as an internal suspicion; I upgraded it to a **sourced third-party fact** via Vibe (Preezy Brown, 2025-08-18, read through the Yahoo syndication since Vibe tollbit-redirects). No source anywhere connects or separates the two aunts. If they are the same person the ending is not just wrong but tonally painful; if not, it stands as written. This cannot be closed from the public record.

Four other findings worth flagging to whoever routes the jury:

- **DISP-01 resolved against the entity-gap packet.** Its content-requirement #5 ("student in the inaugural 2025 class") is false — his own channel published *Being A Professor At Streamer University* on 2025-05-23, verified live with yt-dlp. I also traced the packet's error to its root: 2026 roster press copy reads "returning as a professor after his acceptance into last year's inaugural class." The draft is correct; acting on the packet would inject a false claim.
- **DISP-03 — the draft under-claims against its own citation.** It says "no public source establishes the link" between cousin Dee and DeeBlock, but Sportskeeda — the source it cites for that very beat — describes the shirt as bearing the cousin's face *and* the words "DeeBlock."
- **CLM-11b** — "risk my freedom for the content" is attributed to Vibe, but that sentence isn't in the Vibe text; it traces to other outlets. Substance real, attribution likely wrong.
- **Verified clean:** the corpus stat is exact (409 / creator-media 90 / Eights 11 / Sevens 22 / Threes 21), the rizz percentages are correctly used (80% is the base/male figure; the draft rightly avoids the 90% white-subgroup figure), and every 2018-transcript quote in the Army spine recovered by direct grep — including the "three years vs four years" contradiction in the tape, which Wikipedia resolves in the draft's favor.

I wrote only `evidence-packet.md`; no other file was touched.

